🚀 KPI - Key Performance Indicator
----------------------------------
A KPI is a measurable value used to evaluate business performance against a specific objective.
Not every metric is necessarily a KPI.
For Example.
Quantity Sold is a metric
But, Sales Growth % could be KPI used by management to evaluate performance.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 Metric vs KPI
Metric
A Measurement
Example : total orders = 10,000

KPI
A measurement tied to a business objective.
Example: Sales Growth = +12%
The KPI tells management whether performance is improving or declining

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 why KPI Definition is Critical
Remember your Day 2 Problem: Different users use different logic
This is exactly why we need a KPI Definition 
Suppose sales team says:
Revenue = Gross Sales
Finance says:
Revenue = Gross Sales - Returns
Dashboard Says: 
Revenue = Sales - Discount

Now we have three numbers
This destroys trust in the dashboard.
-- Therefore Every important KPI should have agreed business definition 

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 KPI Definition Template

For every KPI, document:

KPI Name
Business Definition
Formula
Business Purpose
Data Source
Grain
Filters
Owner
Refresh Frequency

Example:
KPI : Total Sales
Business Definition : Total value of sales generated during the selected period
Formula : SUM(Sales_Amount)
Business Purpose : Measure overall sales performance
Data Source : fact_Sales
Dashboard usage : Executive Dashboard, Sales Dashboard, Store Dashboard

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 RETAILMART CORE KPIs
***************************
KPI 1 - Total Sales
Definition - Total sales generated during the selected period
Formula : Total Sales = SUM(Sales_amount)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
KPI 2 - Total Orders
Definition - Number of unique customer orders/transactions
Depending on the data model
Total orders = COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) 

Important
Don't automatically use:

COUNT(*)
because one order can contain multiple products.

Example:
Order 1001 → Product A
Order 1001 → Product B
Order 1001 → Product C

There are:
3 rows
1 order

Therefore:
COUNT(*) = 3
COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) = 1

This is a very common interview issue.
-------------------------------------------------------------------
KPI 3 — Quantity Sold
Quantity Sold = SUM(quantity)

Example:
Product A → 10
Product B → 20
Product C → 15
Total Quantity = 45

--------------------------------------------------------------
KPI 4 — Total Profit
Total Profit =
SUM(sales_amount - cost_amount)

Or, if profit_amount already exists:

Total Profit = SUM(profit_amount)
Important architecture decision

Prefer defining the business logic consistently in the governed transformation/modeling layer rather than calculating the same KPI differently in every Tableau workbook.
---------------------------------------------------------------------
KPI 5 — Profit Margin %
Profit Margin % =
Total Profit / Total Sales × 100

Example:
Sales  = ₹10,00,000
Profit = ₹2,00,000

Profit Margin = 2,00,000 / 10,00,000 × 100
= 20%

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
KPI 6 — Average Order Value

AOV is extremely useful in retail.

AOV = Total Sales / Total Orders

Example:
Sales = ₹10,00,000
Orders = 5,000

AOV = ₹200

It answers: How much does the average customer order generate?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KPI CATALOGUE

| KPI                 | Formula                       | Business Purpose                  |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Total Sales         | `SUM(sales_amount)`           | Measure revenue/sales performance |
| Total Orders        | `COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)`    | Measure transaction volume        |
| Quantity Sold       | `SUM(quantity)`               | Measure units sold                |
| Total Profit        | `SUM(profit_amount)`          | Measure profitability             |
| Profit Margin %     | Profit / Sales × 100          | Measure profitability efficiency  |
| AOV                 | Sales / Orders                | Measure average transaction value |
| Sales Growth %      | Current vs Previous           | Measure growth                    |
| Return Rate %       | Returns / Orders × 100        | Monitor returns                   |
| Customer Count      | `COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id)` | Measure customer base             |
| Repeat Customer %   | Repeat / Total × 100          | Measure customer loyalty          |
| Inventory Available | `SUM(stock_quantity)`         | Monitor stock                     |
| Stock-Out Rate %    | OOS / Active Products × 100   | Monitor availability              |

